---
title: HexaPDF 1.9.0 - Text shaping et al.
created_at: 2026-06-07 13:30:00 +02:00
---

There hasn't been a news entry for quite some time. So this post details the newest changes in
HexaPDF 1.9.0 as well as higlights some of the more important ones of the past releases.

The most notable additions and changes of 1.9.0 are:

* The document layout engine now supports text shaping by using the great HarfBuzz library! This
  means that by using a TrueType font and setting the new
  [`shaping_engine`][HexaPDF::Layout::Style#shaping_engine] style property it is now possible to use
  all OpenType features a font provides.

  The following image illustrates the difference (above without, below with HarfBuzz):

  ![Sample text shaping image](assets/text-shaping.png)

  This will now allow a wide range of scripts to be correctly shown.

* The [HexaPDF::Layout::TableBox] now supports breaking table cells. This means that very high cells
  don't lead to a fit error anymore.

* The [ink annotation][HexaPDF::Type::Annotations::Ink] (sometimes called "scribble" annotation) is
  now supported, including appearance generation.


Additionally, HexaPDF gained some other nice features recently:

* Importing pages is now possible with a [special task][HexaPDF::Task::ImportPages] that supports
  preserving the optional content configuration and interactive form fields.

* There is now a [`Page#extract_text`][HexaPDF::Type::Page#extract_text] method (see
  [HexaPDF::Content::SmartTextExtractor] for details) for extracting the text from pages that
  preserves the overall layout of the text.

* The annotation types [Polygon][HexaPDF::Type::Annotations::Polygon],
  [Polyline][HexaPDF::Type::Annotations::Polyline], [Square][HexaPDF::Type::Annotations::Square],
  [Circle][HexaPDF::Type::Annotations::Circle], and [Line][HexaPDF::Type::Annotations::Line] are
  fully supported with appearance generation.


As always, have a look at the [changelog] for an overview of all changes.

